11
00:45:02,857 --> 00:45:08,857
Sharknado is a 2013 American made-for-television science
fiction comedy disaster film directed by Anthony C.

12
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:14,571
It tells about a waterspout that lifts sharks out of the
ocean and deposits them in Los Angeles.

13
00:53:14,285 --> 00:53:20,285
It is the first installment in the Sharknado film series.

14
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
The movie first aired on the Syfy channel on July 11, 2013, and
stars Tara Reid, Ian Ziering, and John Heard.

15
01:01:25,714 --> 01:01:31,714
It was also given a one-night-only special midnight theatrical screening via Regal
Cinemas and Fathom Events, where it earned $200,000 from 200 screenings.

16
01:05:31,428 --> 01:05:37,428
The over-the-top premise and theatrics of the film
quickly earned it a cult following.

17
01:09:37,142 --> 01:09:43,142
The film spawned a franchise of the same name; five sequels have been produced (Sharknado 2: The Second One, Sharknado 3: Oh Hell No!, Sharknado: The 4th Awakens, Sharknado 5:
Global Swarming, and The Last Sharknado: It's About Time), as well as three spin-off films (Lavalantula, Sharknado: Heart of Sharkness, and 2 Lava 2 Lantula).

18
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
Though the original film was not explicitly a comedy, maintaining at least a façade of
seriousness despite the implausible plot, the sequels were more openly comedic in nature.

19
01:17:48,571 --> 01:17:54,571
The film explores themes of california, helicopter, beach, tornado, hurricane.

20
01:21:54,285 --> 01:22:00,285
The tone is lighthearted and dark and thought_provoking.
